nodecode-tam is a rewrite of vbcherepanov's vbcherepanov/hermes-tam-memory:

  https://github.com/vbcherepanov/hermes-tam-memory
  commit 9a6e51839fb0619c6e41804ac201272e857ea825
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Vitalii Cherepanov (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the two tools the original gave its harness (tam_recall,
tam_save) and the MCP calls behind them -- memory_recall and memory_save, with
the arguments the original sends and the shapes it reads back (a local server
grouping hits by type, a team server answering a ranked list with an author) --
as Common Lisp calling a TAM server over HTTP with the image's own HTTP call,
plus a /tam command, a manual topic and the same two calls from eval.

What was left out, and why: the original's local mode, which spawns the `tam`
binary and speaks MCP over stdio, because a cell that reads a process's pipes is
a second transport to carry and to test; the cell talks to the HTTP endpoint
both server kinds already serve. Also left out: the per-turn auto-capture and
auto-recall the original hooks into its harness's turn, which Nodecode's own
shipped memory cell covers for its turns, and the mirroring of that harness's
built-in memory writes, which does not exist here. Nothing of the original's
code is bundled: this is a reimplementation against the same MCP surface.
